From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HOTTY Agent <hotty@neuroplast.io>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 19:17:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 24/24] hottyterm: the macOS menu sees keys as key-remap makes
 them; no Mac keys for quit, close or full screen

The maintainer, 2026-10-10: kill Cmd+Q, Cmd+W and Ctrl+Cmd+F on the Mac
too, and swap Cmd and Ctrl in hottyterm as Option and Alt are swapped.
Ghostty's key-remap swaps them (`key-remap = super=ctrl`, `key-remap =
ctrl=super`), but AppKit's menu matched keys before the remap: the main
key, which reaches macOS as Cmd, still hit Copy, Select All, Hide and
Minimize with C, A, H and M instead of reaching the terminal as Ctrl.

The menu now sees a key as remapped. A key that becomes no Command key
is the terminal's, never the menu's; one that becomes a Command key goes
to the menu as that, to the menu item of its binding or to the menu's
own items (Hide, Minimize). ghostty_surface_key_remap_mods gives Swift
the remapped modifiers.

The default keys for quit, close (Cmd+W) and full screen are gone on
the Mac too, the menu's static Ctrl+Cmd+F with them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
